Audit pose with the Film Stock choice first placed after the look line (JournalFlowTests 16mm-title-accessibility-largest,
held drags until the Film title heading is whole on screen): light flagged "Color" {{34.0, 91.0}, {334.0, 71.3}}, half under
the navigation bar (bar bottom 189 pt); dark flagged "Color" and the "Film Stock" heading {{32.0, 17.7}, {233.3, 63.3}}; and one
later dark run stopped 73 pt further, with "Color" {{34.0, 19.7}} wholly and "Black and white" {{34.0, 93.0}, {334.0, 133.3}}
half under the bar. All measure at least 9.12:1 at rest (above), so each finding was the bar's blur, but which short control
rests there changed from run to run. Before slice 3 the 589 pt look line filled that region whatever the pose.
Decision: the choice now sits before the look lines (it also reads as choose, then see what each stock develops like).
The single 589 pt 16mm look line then caused an elementless clipped-text finding at the Load Film button audit, so the look
became two short lines; the second, "Highlight glow: red on color, neutral on black and white", rests under the bar at the
title pose, and the one exception names it.

